{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "y2xNdf",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Ajustes",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "X8ZiJF",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Ajustes — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "O572gY",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "One Ajustes, no admin zone. On a single-user instance the /admin split is a costume (D5): the same person owns the account and the box, so the design merges /profile and /admin into one hub with sections.\n\nThe scope shrank twice on its way here: D9 moved the asset catalogue to Activos › Rastreados, and D16 reduced the notification panel to the two channels that actually deliver. What is left: cuenta, apariencia y región, avisos, instancia, datos.\n\nScreens: Ajustes (hub) · Integraciones · Registros · Instancia.\n\nGrounding: /profile tabs (información, apariencia+región, notificaciones, seguridad, datos y sesión) · admin/integrations 'Conectividad de mercado' with one key per provider · admin/logs 'Registros · últimos 90 días' · admin/settings SiteConfig toggles audited through SiteConfigChange · Mission Control at /admin/jobs.\n\n⚠ Two of the three SiteConfig toggles are drawn as if they worked, and today they do not: auto_sync_enabled and email_notifications_enabled persist, are audited, and have no consumer — the jobs and the mailers never read them (D17). maintenance_mode is real, enforced in ApplicationController.\n\n⚠ D18 is REVERSED (2026-08-26 → ADR-015): one key per provider. The provider audit found that four sources — Alpaca, Massive (ex-Polygon), Finnhub and CoinGecko — explicitly prohibit using several credentials to exceed a free tier. The multi-key count and the rotation note are gone from this artboard; the fallback that remains is across sources, not across keys of one source, which is what GatewayChain already does.\n\nDesktop (1280, kit 0.5.0): Hub, Integraciones and Estado y mantenimiento. Registros is NOT drawn — it is a list and reflows; a real desktop log TABLE would be a new component, so it waits for a decision rather than being invented here.\n\nDesktop findings (2026-08-24, panel C1/C5/C4): (a) the Hub splits into two semantic columns — cuenta y preferencias | instancia y datos — not an arbitrary half; (b) the Tema and Moneda segmented controls were stretching to the 476 column and are pinned to their native 342. A control is not a container: it should never absorb the width it is given. That is the kit gap logged in 0.5.0, and this is its first real case; (c) Integraciones as a 3x2 grid puts the quota bars side by side, so Alpha Vantage's 25 calls/day and Polygon's 5/min stop being isolated facts and become a comparable budget (C1) — the same argument that earns Rastreados its own desktop artboard in assets.pen.\n\n🔴 Desktop makes the D17 lie LOUDER, not quieter. On mobile the three toggles are a block you scroll past; here they get a column of their own, opposite the diagnostics, which reads as the control panel of the instance. Two of the three still do nothing. Wiring auto_sync_enabled and email_notifications_enabled was already a precondition for building this screen (CODE_CHANGES §8) — this layout raises the cost of ignoring it.\n\nCopy: es-MX. kit-version-source 0.5.0.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
